>
<p>A professional website audit connects a defined business question to reproducible evidence and a prioritised action plan. The report should explain what was checked, what was observed and how each completed fix will be verified.</p>
<p>Professional quality comes from method and evidence. A paid logo or long report does not establish that quality.</p>

<h2 id="what-makes-it-professional">What makes a website audit professional?</h2>
<p>A professional audit has explicit scope, traceable evidence, justified priorities and documented limits. Recommendations identify affected pages and the conditions needed to verify resolution.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scope:</strong> properties, pages, systems, dates and exclusions.</li>
  <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> source, observation, sample and access limits.</li>
  <li><strong>Priority:</strong> impact, effort, dependencies and confidence.</li>
  <li><strong>Handoff:</strong> recommended change, owner and acceptance check.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="diy-tools-vs-expert-review">How does expert review differ from audit tools?</h2>
<p>Audit tools collect repeatable signals at scale. Expert review chooses the right evidence, validates warnings, identifies likely causes and orders work against the buyer's objective.</p>
<p>The <a href="/free-website-audit/">AuditWeb free checker</a> reviews pasted HTML locally. It cannot crawl a domain or measure live speed, security, accessibility or indexation. Use a professional review when the decision needs those broader evidence sources.</p>

<h2 id="whats-included">What should a professional audit include?</h2>
<p>The quote should name the review areas and deliverables. Common areas include search access, on-page content, performance, mobile journeys, accessibility observations and authorised public security checks.</p>
<p>Google's <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing">crawling and indexing documentation</a> shows why robots access, canonical signals and indexing evidence need separate tests. A report should avoid collapsing them into one health score.</p>
<p>Read the <a href="/website-audit-services/report-example/">completed audit report example</a> to inspect a practical finding format.</p>

<h2 id="how-to-choose-an-auditor">How should you choose an auditor?</h2>
<p>Choose an auditor by reviewing a sample, method and proposed scope. Ask who performs the work and who checks the findings.</p>
<p>For a focused investigation led by one specialist, use the <a href="/website-audit-services/consultant/">website audit consultant selection guide</a> to compare expertise, continuity and handoff responsibilities.</p>
<ol>
  <li>Compare the exact pages, systems and data sources included.</li>
  <li>Check that sample findings include evidence and verification.</li>
  <li>Confirm data access, storage and deletion requirements.</li>
  <li>Confirm report format, meetings, revisions, price and date.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="getting-value-from-your-report">How do you get value from the report?</h2>
<p>Turn accepted findings into owned implementation tasks. Give each task an assignee, dependency, acceptance check and evidence record.</p>
<p>Measure later outcomes against a dated baseline and the same definition. Search, performance and conversion results can also change because of releases, campaigns or seasonality.</p>

<h2 id="red-flags">Which audit-service claims are red flags?</h2>
<p>Question guaranteed rankings, fixed revenue gains, unsupported client counts and tool scores presented as independent evidence. Also question a provider that cannot state which pages or systems the price covers.</p>
<p>Google says a sitemap can help discovery but does not guarantee indexing in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/help/crawling-index-faq">crawling and indexing FAQ</a>. An auditor should not guarantee search-engine decisions.</p>

<h2 id="our-approach">What is AuditWeb's professional audit approach?</h2>
<p>AuditWeb starts with the site, business question, priority pages and available data. Basic audits start at $297 USD and comprehensive audits start at $997 USD. Complex work is quoted.</p>
<p>The written quote confirms scope, evidence sources, deliverables, price, date and follow-up. Implementation and ongoing monitoring require a separate agreement.</p>
